ArrivalCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation runs the Arrival Control as soon as the Transporter driving freely within the area arrives
at the Marker designated by <Path>.
For an omnidirectional Marker Plant Simulation runs the control once the Transporter driving freely
within the area arrives at the half-way point of the curvature/fillet at the Marker.
If you did not specify a Method, the value of the attribute is VOID.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ArrivalCtrl:method
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
MyMarker.ArrivalCtrl := &myMethod
See also
Arrival Control [Marker]
ArrivalCtrl [SimTalk]
